+
+## Externally started native generations
+
+An external calendar can reuse a Temporal workflow ID across native generations.
+For native ingress whose RunRequest.run_id is empty, new histories record the
+`runengine.native-root-identity.v1` patch and expose an opaque TemporalRunIdentity
+through coordination operations. Child operation identities then include that
+generation. Requests submitted through RunHost retain their existing logical IDs.
+Older histories without the marker retain their original behavior on replay.
+
+`TemporalRunHost.get_pinned_handle(identity)` addresses one workflow/run/namespace
+for results, status, messages, events, children, and cancellation. It rejects a
+namespace mismatch before requesting a handle. Ordinary `get_handle(str)` keeps
+interpreting every string as an ordinary workflow ID; it does not reserve an ID
+prefix or silently redirect an existing run. Integrations decide explicitly when
+an opaque value is a native identity. The existing TemporalEnvironmentOwner name
+remains an import alias, and its encoded journal format is unchanged.
